WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.760
The CIS Controls include Implementation Groups, often called IG1, IG2, and IG3.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.850
These groups help organizations prioritize activities based on risk, complexity,

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:11.400
and available resources.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.700
Smaller organizations often begin with IG1,

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:18.525
while larger or more complex environments may implement additional safeguards.

00:00:18.525 --> 00:00:21.560
Implementation Groups recognize that organizations have different needs and maturity

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:22.020
levels.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:25.520
A small team with limited resources may need a different starting point than a large

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.495
enterprise with complex systems.

00:00:27.495 --> 00:00:29.380
This structure helps make the controls practical.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:32.980
It gives organizations a way to sequence improvement without losing sight of long-term

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:33.580
maturity.
